<title>USA: Motorola unit gets $4 mln FLEX contract.</title>
<headline>Motorola unit gets $4 mln FLEX contract.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Advanced Messaging Group said on Thursday it received a $4 million FLEX protocol-based infrastructure contract with Puerto Rico Telephone Co.</p>
<p>Puerto Rico Telephone was expanding and upgrading its existing paging system to be 100 percent FLEX-capable, the Motorola unit said in a statement.</p>
<p>The upgrade included the purchase of more than 100 Nucleus II transmitters, the company said.</p>
<p>Puerto Rican Telephone was a leading paging carrier in Latin America.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
